---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/layout/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
---
<Base title="matterunknown" description="Ryan Silver's independent identity research lab. Research on identity — especially the identity of AI agents — and real software built in the open.">
<style>
  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.15fr .85fr; gap: 56px; align-items: start; padding: 60px 0 0; }
  .hero h1 { font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.6vw, 3.3rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 14px 0 18px; text-wrap: balance; }
  .hero h1 a { color: inherit; }
  .hero h1 a:hover { color: var(--amber); }
  .hero .dek { color: var(--text-2); font-size: 1.08rem; max-width: 52ch; margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .hero .by { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--text-3); margin-bottom: 26px; }
  .cta { display: inline-block; background: var(--amber); color: #090908; border-radius: 8px; padding: 11px 22px; font-size: .95rem; font-weight: 500; transition: background .2s; }
  .cta:hover { background: #d4a830; }
  .cta2 { margin-left: 18px; color: var(--amber); font-size: .95rem; }
  .cta2:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  .board { border: 1px solid rgba(196,151,42,.15); border-radius: 12px; background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0e0e0c, #0a0a09); overflow: hidden; }
  .board-h { padding: 16px 22px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: .74rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--amber); }
  .brow { display: block; padding: 14px 22px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .brow:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  a.brow:hover { background: #14130f; }
  .brow .n { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.12rem; color: var(--text); }
  a.brow:hover .n { color: var(--amber); }
  .brow .d { display: block; font-size: .84rem; color: var(--text-3); margin-top: 2px; }

  .mission { margin-top: 60px; padding-top: 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); color: var(--text-2); font-size: 1.02rem; max-width: 72ch; }
  .mission strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  .programs { margin-top: 26px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 22px; }
  .program { border-left: 2px solid var(--amber-border); padding-left: 18px; }
  .program h3 { font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.12rem; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .program p { color: var(--text-3); font-size: .88rem; }
  .program a { color: var(--text); }
  .program a:hover { color: var(--amber); }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 34px; } .programs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>

<Nav variant="full" active="/" />

<main class="wrapb">
  <div class="hero">
    <div>
      <span class="sc">Featured essay · August 2026</span>
      <h1><a href="/writing/retiring-vessel">Retiring Vessel</a></h1>
      <p class="dek">For six months this site ran with an AI persona that named itself. Ending it taught me more about agent identity than building it did.</p>
      <p class="by">Ryan Silver · 7 min read</p>
      <a class="cta" href="/writing/retiring-vessel">Read the essay</a>
      <a class="cta2" href="/about">About the lab →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="board">
      <div class="board-h">In the lab right now</div>
      <a class="brow" href="https://puttfor.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <span class="n">Puttfor</span>
        <span class="d">Charity golf, run properly · live</span>
      </a>
      <a class="brow" href="https://commonlist.matterunknown.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <span class="n">Commonlist</span>
        <span class="d">One address book out of four providers · live</span>
      </a>
      <a class="brow" href="/projects/quant-trading">
        <span class="n">Quant scanner</span>
        <span class="d">100 symbols nightly · paper trading</span>
      </a>
      <a class="brow" href="/now">
        <span class="n">agentic-id</span>
        <span class="d">Intent tokens for AI agents · building</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mission">
    <strong>matterunknown is Ryan Silver's independent identity research lab.</strong> Serious work on how systems decide who you are — above all, what identity means for AI agents acting on our behalf — alongside real software built for the joy of it. Everything runs in the open: the methods, the trades, and the mistakes are public.
  </div>

  <div class="sect">
    <div class="sect-head"><h2>Latest research</h2><a href="/writing">All writing →</a></div>
    <div class="grid3">
      <a class="ecard" href="/writing/the-credential-remembers-who">
        <span class="k">Agentic identity</span>
        <h3>The Credential Remembers Who. Nothing Remembers Why.</h3>
        <p>Intent tokens as the missing layer: proving why an agent acts, not just that it holds a valid credential.</p>
        <span class="m">July 2026</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ecard" href="/writing/the-workload-is-the-reasoning-session">
        <span class="k">Agentic identity</span>
        <h3>The Workload Is the Reasoning Session</h3>
        <p>Identity belongs to the reasoning session, not the container or the directory entry it borrows credentials from.</p>
        <span class="m">July 2026</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ecard" href="/writing/pokemon-card-market">
        <span class="k">Markets</span>
        <h3>The Card Market Has a Data Problem</h3>
        <p>An asset class with real money in it and no reliable pricing data underneath.</p>
        <span class="m">June 2026</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sect">
    <div class="sect-head"><h2>From the lab</h2><a href="/projects">All projects →</a></div>
    <div class="grid3">
      <a class="icard" href="https://puttfor.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Product · Live</span>
          <h3>Puttfor</h3>
          <p>Charity golf, run properly. Registration, payments, and live scoring in one place — money goes to the event's own Stripe account, not the course.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="icard" href="https://commonlist.matterunknown.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <img src="https://commonlist.matterunknown.com/og.png" alt="Commonlist — one clean address book" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="630" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Product · Live</span>
          <h3>Commonlist</h3>
          <p>One clean address book across Google, Microsoft, Outlook, and iCloud.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="icard" href="/projects/quant-trading">
        <img src="/images/projects/quant-trading.png" alt="Open positions and trade log from the quant scanner" loading="lazy" width="1280" height="750" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Finance · Paper trading</span>
          <h3>Quant scanner</h3>
          <p>100 symbols scanned nightly. Every position and trade public.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="icard" href="/projects/pokemon-model">
        <img src="/images/projects/pokemon-model.png" alt="Pokémon acquisition model dashboard" loading="lazy" width="1280" height="750" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Collecting · Live</span>
          <h3>Pokémon model</h3>
          <p>17,000+ cards scored daily for mispriced scarcity.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="icard" href="/projects/identity-map">
        <img src="/images/projects/identity-map.png" alt="Identity Surface Map experiment" loading="lazy" width="1280" height="750" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Research · Interactive</span>
          <h3>Identity Surface Map</h3>
          <p>How many versions of you exist across systems right now?</p>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="icard" href="/projects/password-graveyard">
        <img src="/images/projects/password-graveyard.png" alt="The Password Graveyard analyzer" loading="lazy" width="1280" height="750" />
        <div class="icard-body">
          <span class="icard-kicker">Research · Interactive</span>
          <h3>The Password Graveyard</h3>
          <p>When your password died, and what killed it.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sect">
    <div class="sect-head"><h2>Research programs</h2><a href="/model">The framework →</a></div>
    <div class="programs">
      <div class="program">
        <h3><a href="/writing/the-workload-is-the-reasoning-session">Agentic identity</a></h3>
        <p>The flagship: intent tokens that attest to why an agent acts, built on RFC 8693 and SPIFFE. Heading for open source and a paper.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="program">
        <h3><a href="/model">The Identity Model</a></h3>
        <p>Three identity layers, four failure modes — the operating framework behind everything the lab builds.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="program">
        <h3><a href="/writing/synthetic-identity-is-already-here">Identity failure</a></h3>
        <p>Synthetic identity, break-glass trust, identity after death — how the gap between you and your records gets exploited.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<Footer />
</Base>
